<Base title="About" description="About The Scapegoat Daughter — anonymous essays on complex trauma and family dynamics.">
  <article class="about-content prose">
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p>
      I write anonymously because the stories I tell are not only mine. They belong to a family system
      that would rather they stayed buried. But silence is its own kind of inheritance, and I've decided
      to stop passing it down.
    </p>
    <p>
      These essays explore what it means to grow up as the designated problem in a family that couldn't
      face its own. They are about complex trauma, emotional neglect, scapegoating, and the slow,
      unglamorous work of becoming a person outside the role you were assigned.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am not a therapist. I'm just someone trying to make sense of things, one essay at a time.
    </p>
    <p>
      If any of this resonates, you're not alone.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
